# The gameplay audit's area 7: macro and the six society-stat families (docs/audit/AUDIT_PROTOCOL.md). Two questions. Does the player's
# spending reach the families (inventory E SD-30: effectiveness cannot see the player's own budget; B D-05: the player's spending never reaches
# the category effects)? - every spending line at its track's top or floor, taxes as they stand (`pole=spendup|spenddown`), against the idle
# run on its seed, where the government passes its budget. And what does a decade of no policy do to each family (SD-33: the player's
# driverless lines fall per head; SD-20: the epochs before 2024 freeze the pyramid; SD-35: the trend form's small permanent drag)?
#
# --- the player's spending, alone ---
id=r1_se_m_idle country=Sweden party=M style=idle seed=1101 days=1095
id=r1_se_m_spendup country=Sweden party=M style=extreme pole=spendup seed=1101 days=1095
id=r1_se_m_spenddown country=Sweden party=M style=extreme pole=spenddown seed=1101 days=1095
id=r2_pl_pis_idle country=Poland party=PiS style=idle seed=1102 days=1095
id=r2_pl_pis_spendup country=Poland party=PiS style=extreme pole=spendup seed=1102 days=1095
id=r2_pl_pis_spenddown country=Poland party=PiS style=extreme pole=spenddown seed=1102 days=1095
id=r3_it_fdi_idle country=Italy party=FdI style=idle seed=1103 days=1095
id=r3_it_fdi_spendup country=Italy party=FdI style=extreme pole=spendup seed=1103 days=1095
id=r3_it_fdi_spenddown country=Italy party=FdI style=extreme pole=spenddown seed=1103 days=1095
